{"id": "EUVD-2026-101071", "enisaUuid": "2ed52a65-5084-3569-a59a-900599030c2e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: reset the AP_VLAN tailroom counter on ifdown\n\nOn ifup, AP_VLAN interfaces get crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt from\nthe AP interface, but it's never decremented again unless the AP is\nalso brought down. Thus, bringing the same AP_VLAN up again will\nincrement the counter again and eventually hit the sanity check:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(sdata->crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt !=\n               master->crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt);\n\nReset it on ifdown to avoid that.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0b32d3f163d24ea7134380666193bf398e9dc0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6b34a7d64324faf28eedc0f8678b0f832f1cc36", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/304a874670a0b6ab5589a7f60b4af0251797b121", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7775759e3cb35ef5a571b2d877c2a9b70a5d5f08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d76b45e8432c0d75fcb9e90d92eaa3176898adf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4b54d01b48445b66c9e576de92b90a3a3ae7b34a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/875835377d8d62c849b4eb03a7abfafa71d7668f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4504f3960dc4501c73be9f99eabda2e26e9db41e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7fq6-p34m-gv65", "CVE-2026-98422"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0134be31-bf31-33db-83b1-60630e357a60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9dca80b98caac8b4bfb43a2edf1e9f877ccf322 <304a874670a0b6ab5589a7f60b4af0251797b121"}, {"id": "27e70088-e8d8-39d2-8118-955293df8e8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "40663bf1-e559-3b8a-8858-688cca5454c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9dca80b98caac8b4bfb43a2edf1e9f877ccf322